  "summary": "I am the AN/TPY-2 Radar Agile Product Owner (PO) for the Jaguar Software Release and Tactical Installations Team. I lead a team that plays a crucial role in ensuring that software is delivered efficiently, reliably, and aligned with business goals. As a PO I am responsible for overseeing the entire lifecycle of software delivery, ensuring compliance with contractual requirements, and optimizing delivery and installation processes. My role involves coordinating with cross-functional teams, managing backlogs, and aligning business and technical priorities to deliver high-quality and on-time compliant software and documentation. I ensure a smooth and efficient software delivery and installation. I bridge the gap between business delivery dates and support teams such as QE, Safety, CM, DM, String and document control ensuring that high quality software is released, packaged, audited, distributed and installed efficiently, timely and reliably. My scope covers Software Release publishing, release pipeline automation, packaging, CDRL SVDs, SW Assurance, build delta change reports, delta changes verification for QE readiness, build SLOC metrics and reports, media generation, media distribution, audits and installations while supporting Agile development methodologies and driving the efficient and secure release of software to customers. I love and enjoy my job. \n\nSpecialties: SME (Subject Matter Expert) on: Linux shell scripting languages, Linux OS, Smartbear Collaborator, Agile, Git, Bitbucket, Artifactory, SVDs, CM, SW development, Automation, Test, Quality, Release, Installations and Deployment.",
