      "description": "+ Celebrating 30 Years in Engineering ✨\n\nYesterday 9/12/25 marked a very special milestone for me — 30 years of service as an engineer. Over the past three decades, I’ve had the privilege of working on challenging projects, learning from talented colleagues, and contributing to innovations that make a difference and save lifes.\n\nOver the decades, I’ve witnessed amazing times for technology and engineering — from rapid innovation and new frontiers in design to breakthroughs that have transformed how we live and work. It has been a privilege to contribute to that progress, side by side with talented colleagues and mentors who shaped my journey.\n\nOne of the greatest rewards has been the opportunity to pay it forward — mentoring and guiding the next generation of engineers and leaders. To my team of new leaders: you are the future. Watching you step up with confidence, take ownership, make decisions and grow into your roles is both inspiring and motivating. I see my legacy not just in the projects delivered, but in the leaders I’ve had the honor to mentor and develop.\n\nBut beyond the code, systems, and releases, the true highlight has been the people. I’ve had the privilege to mentor new leaders, to learn from brilliant colleagues, and to see ideas turn into solutions that make a real impact. For me, the legacy is not just the technology built, but the leaders and teams who will carry it forward.\n\nI hope my legacy is measured not only in the solutions I’ve built, but in the growth of those I’ve worked with.\n\nFor me, this milestone is not just about looking back —it’s about building a legacy that lives on through innovation, teamwork, and leadership.\n\nTo my Jaguar agile team you make me proud. Your excellence, commitment, creativity, trust and collaboration make every achievement possible. Wow!\n\nHere’s to the past 30 years, and to an even brighter future for technology, engineering, and the leaders who will carry it forward. \n🚀 Let's #KeepRockin' 🚀🔧\n--with love,Marlyn",
      "insights": ""
     }
